lab-process-mail now carries the procedure for answering the list in
its own prompt, and runs it from an installed copy the agent cannot
edit. Keeping the skill as well would leave two copies of the same
procedure to drift apart, and the in-tree one is exactly what a pass
could change under the loop.

CLAUDE.md points at the tool and its prompt instead, so a session
answering the list by hand follows the same steps a pass does.
